MapQuest Open Directions (mapquest-open-directions) mentions routing between latitude/longitude points and includes driving, walking, biking, and transit. It supports international use and is based on OpenStreetMap data, which includes country boundaries.

Therefore, for great circle approximation, these mapping APIs may help.

To identify the countries overflown, some kind of polygon intersection or lookup in country polygons is necessary.

Hence, geonames or openstreetmap (mapping category) may assist in matching coordinates to countries.

